 "verdicts": {
  "In Temporal, GPU-bound or side-effecting operations (vLLM inference, fine-tuning, embeddings) should go in activities, not workflow code, because workflow code must be deterministic and replays on every worker restart.": 1,
  "Inngest checkpoints each step.run() output; on failure it re-invokes the function and returns cached results for completed steps.": 1,
  "Restate assigns each virtual object a unique key (e.g. a session ID), serializes handler calls on it, and journals each ctx.run() before execution, giving exactly-once semantics without application-level idempotency keys.": 1
 }
